__pycache__/
*.pyc
data/*.sqlite3
.venv/
runs/
.DS_Store
downloads/

# Benchmark geometry is NOT redistributed (workshop terms), but its record is.
# Gap J5: with the whole directory ignored, the KCS "-0.09% on displacement"
# validation silently skipped on every machine but the one that generated the
# file, and nothing in the repo said what the missing file should have been.
# The pattern must be `dir/*`, not `dir/`: git will not re-include a path
# inside a directory it has already excluded.
data/benchmark_geom/*
!data/benchmark_geom/CHECKSUMS.json

# BUILD ARTIFACTS, gap J6. `data/exports/hull.{iges,step}` are REGENERATED by
# the test suite on every run, so tracking them dirtied the tree constantly —
# they were re-modified by 5 of the last 10 commits, caused cherry-pick
# conflicts, and provoked an unasked `git checkout --` by another agent.
# `renders/` held 9 committed PNGs (~2.3 MB) of CFD output that is reproducible
# from the runs.
data/exports/
renders/

badFaces
illegalFaces
selfInterPoints.obj
*.obj

# The evolution spine keeps a machine-local, append-only history:
#   data/evolution/archive.jsonl  every genome, every state change
#   data/evolution/gaps.jsonl     the live gap queue
# Gitignored for the same reason as data/exports/ and renders/ (gap J6): a
# file the test suite rewrites on every run dirties the tree constantly and
# conflicts on every cherry-pick. It is one machine's own history, not a
# shared artefact -- the record that must survive is docs/GAP-REGISTER.md.
#
# TRACKING gaps.jsonl WAS PROPOSED 2026-08-07 AND REJECTED, deliberately. The
# finding was real -- a fresh clone has no queue and none of the 83 recorded
# closures -- but the file is the wrong fix for it:
#   - the log is DERIVED. Every closure in it was written by --apply from a
#     predicate over code that is already tracked, so committing it stores a
#     conclusion beside its own evidence (a number declared twice, this
#     codebase's recurring defect) and the log is the copy that goes stale.
#   - it cannot be merged. It is append-only, four records per closure, and
#     GapQueue.next_id mints ids by scanning the log it has: two agents closing
#     two different gaps both mint G-120 and NEITHER side of the merge is
#     right. data/exports/* taught the cheap version of this lesson already.
# What the decision owes instead is reconstructibility and noise, and both are
# now enforced by tests/test_reconcile_gaps.py:
#     python scripts/reconcile_gaps.py --rebuild     # register + predicates
# and an absent queue exits non-zero with a banner rather than reporting an
# empty register as if there were nothing to do.
data/evolution/

# Agent worktrees are scratch checkouts, never content.
.claude/worktrees/

# `scripts/blender_compare.py` writes one STL per arm per hull here: 8 arms x
# 3 hulls is ~1.5 GB, and the largest single file measured is a 232 MB ascii
# STL (the subsurf-1-finecage arm, 1155588 triangles). They are REGENERATED by
# re-running the script and none of them is evidence -- the numbers live in
# docs/research/BLENDER.md. Tracking them would dirty the tree on every run,
# which data/exports/* already taught this repository once.
data/blender/
